<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jean-Louis Ferrand</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1808</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jean-Louis Ferrand was a French general who governed the former Spanish colony of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/santo-domingo">Santo Domingo</a> after French forces withdrew there from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/haiti">Haiti</a> in 1803–1804. He repelled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jean-jacques-dessalines">Jean-Jacques Dessalines</a>' siege of the city in 1805, revived trade and restored <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavery">slavery</a>. When Dominican <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/criollo-people">creoles</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/juan-sanchez-ramirez">Juan Sánchez Ramírez</a> rose in 1808, he was defeated at Palo Hincado and killed himself after the battle.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jean-louis-ferrand.jpg" alt="Jean-Louis Ferrand" width="274" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:G%C3%A9n%C3%A9ral_Jean-Louis_Ferrand.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
